The framework yields a three-part finding. First (Objective A), attention patterns encode biologically structured information with a clean layer-specific organisation—protein–protein interactions in early layers, transcriptional regulation in late layers (exploratory) (Additional file 1: Supplementary Note 17)—and Cell-State Stratified Interpretability (CSSI) exploits this structure to improve curated-reference GRN recovery up to \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
